  "id": "sensory-engineering",
  "term": "sensory engineering",
  "definition": "Sensory engineering is an approach to design research that examines how people’s emotional responses and preferences relate to the sensory or aesthetic features of a product or image. In this context, it is used to map evaluated qualities such as style, color, market appeal, and psychological impression to consumers’ emotional needs.",
